<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Honda Air Blade vs Automatic Scooter: Hanoi Rental Cost Comparison</h1>
<p>The Honda Air Blade rents at a verified 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and a single monthly figure of 1,500,000 VND in Hanoi, confirmed at the counter as one number rather than a range. The automatic scooter is not one machine but a category with two verified tiers: the entry tier of Honda Wave, Yamaha Sirius, Yamaha Mio and Honda Click at 150,000 VND per day, and the step-up tier the Air Blade shares with the Honda Vision and the electric motorbike at 200,000 VND per day. This comparison reads the Air Blade's ladder against the category honestly, including the part most riders miss, which is that the Air Blade is not an alternative to the automatic scooter, it is the step-up tier's standard monthly representative.</p>
<p>We compare the daily, weekly and monthly structures at both tiers, the break-even logic each ladder produces, what the Air Blade's premium actually buys as a ride, who each tier suits, and the deposit, gear and support questions that come with either choice. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, see the full model range at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and check common questions on the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The verified price ladders</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Daily rate comparison</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Weekly and monthly comparison</a></li>
